Subject: [PATCH] select: UNION LIMIT 1 shortcut only with UNION/UNION ALL to its left

multiSelect() codes a compound whose right-most operator is a UNION
with LIMIT 1 (unionWithLimitOne(), SQLITE_UnionLimit) like a UNION ALL:
run the SELECTs to the left with the same LIMIT 1 by a recursive
sqlite3Select(pPrior,&dest), then the right-most SELECT. When the part
to the left contains an EXCEPT or INTERSECT (or a UNION to the left of
a UNION ALL), that recursive call codes it with multiSelectByMerge(),
and two things go wrong:

1. For a materialized subquery, multiSelect() has already turned the
   SRT_EphemTab destination into SRT_Table. Since 456ef2d (2026-10-29,
   "Omit code in generateOutputSubroutine() that is dead due to
   [659805b27cef273d]") generateOutputSubroutine() handles SRT_Table
   only with SQLITE_ENABLE_UPDATE_DELETE_LIMIT, so the merge falls into
   the default case: assert(pDest->eDest==SRT_Output) fails on debug
   builds, and release builds emit the subquery rows as OP_ResultRow
   of the outer statement (with too few registers) and leave the
   materialized table empty:

    CREATE TABLE t1(a); INSERT INTO t1 VALUES(10),(20);
    SELECT * FROM t1 CROSS JOIN
      (SELECT 1 INTERSECT SELECT 1 UNION SELECT 1 LIMIT 1);
    -- release: "1|1"; expected "10|1" and "20|1"

   659805b (fa4cadf) made the plain UNION ALL path use the merge for
   any non-UNION-ALL operator to the left, which is why SRT_Table
   looked dead, but missed the UNION LIMIT 1 path.

2. The left compound coded on its own ignores collating sequences of
   SELECTs further to the right, the problem 659805b fixed for UNION
   ALL (merge1.test 260-310):

    SELECT 'a' EXCEPT SELECT 'A' UNION SELECT 'x' COLLATE NOCASE LIMIT 1;
    -- returns 'a'; the full compound is {'x'}

Fix: take the shortcut only if unionLimitOneLeftOk(): the operators to
the left, right to left, are zero or more UNIONs (each inherits the
LIMIT 1 and takes the shortcut recursively) followed by zero or more
UNION ALLs (no merge needed). Everything else uses the merge, which
handles the LIMIT and collations of the whole compound. An assert() in
the shortcut branch records the invariant. Regression test
test/unionlimit1.sql (CLI .testcase format), which also checks that a
UNION/UNION ALL chain still avoids the MERGE.

Found by the suite's sqlite-ossfuzz_debug module (755-byte fuzzer
input, assert in generateOutputSubroutine()). Changes code generation
in release builds too (wrong-result fix, not only the assert).

Upstream: not reported; not fixed as of dc9b322 (master 2026-11-23), nor
in the sqlite.org timeline up to 2026-11-23 19:49. Introduced by
456ef2d (25ff0ad78e, 2026-10-29) on top of fa4cadf (659805b27c,
2026-10-29, bug 2026-10-21T19:20:14Z); the collation part predates the
shallow history.
---
diff --git a/src/select.c b/src/select.c
index f6fc3ec..59e3a5f 100644
--- a/src/select.c
+++ b/src/select.c
@@ -3067,6 +3067,26 @@ static int unionWithLimitOne(sqlite3 *db, Select *p){
   return 1;
 }
 
+/*
+** Return TRUE if the compound operators to the left of p, taken from
+** right to left, are zero or more UNIONs followed by zero or more
+** UNION ALLs.
+**
+** multiSelect() codes a UNION with LIMIT 1 by running the SELECTs to
+** its left (with the same LIMIT 1) and then the right-most SELECT.  That
+** is only correct if the left part never needs multiSelectByMerge(): a
+** UNION to the left inherits the LIMIT 1 and so takes the same path
+** recursively, and a pure UNION ALL needs no merge at all.  But an
+** EXCEPT or INTERSECT, or a UNION to the left of a UNION ALL, would be
+** coded by multiSelectByMerge() on its own, which (1) ignores collating
+** sequences from SELECTs further to the right and (2) does not handle
+** the SRT_Table destination used for a materialized subquery.
+*/
+static int unionLimitOneLeftOk(Select *p){
+  for(p=p->pPrior; p->pPrior && p->op==TK_UNION; p=p->pPrior){}
+  return selectIsUnionAll(p);
+}
+
 /*
 ** This routine is called to process a compound query formed from
 ** two or more separate queries using UNION, UNION ALL, EXCEPT, or
@@ -3156,7 +3176,9 @@ static int multiSelect(
     /* If the compound has an ORDER BY clause, then always use the merge
     ** algorithm. */
     return multiSelectByMerge(pParse, p, pDest);
-  }else if( !selectIsUnionAll(p) && !unionWithLimitOne(db,p) ){
+  }else if( !selectIsUnionAll(p)
+         && (!unionWithLimitOne(db,p) || !unionLimitOneLeftOk(p))
+  ){
     /* If the compound is EXCEPT, INTERSECT, or UNION (anything other than
     ** UNION ALL) then also always use the merge algorithm.  However, the
     ** multiSelectByMerge() routine requires that the compound have an
@@ -3169,11 +3191,14 @@ static int multiSelect(
     return multiSelectByMerge(pParse, p, pDest);
   }else{
     /* For a UNION ALL compound without ORDER BY, or for a UNION with a 
-    ** LIMIT of exactly 1 and no OFFSET and no ORDER BY, simply run the left
-    ** query, then run the right query */
+    ** LIMIT of exactly 1 and no OFFSET and no ORDER BY (and a suitable
+    ** left part, see unionLimitOneLeftOk()), simply run the left query,
+    ** then run the right query */
     int addr = 0;
     int nLimit = 0;  /* Initialize to suppress harmless compiler warning */
 
+    assert( selectIsUnionAll(p) || unionLimitOneLeftOk(p) );
+
 #ifndef SQLITE_OMIT_EXPLAIN
     if( pPrior->pPrior==0 ){
       ExplainQueryPlan((pParse, 1, "COMPOUND QUERY"));
diff --git a/test/unionlimit1.sql b/test/unionlimit1.sql
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3c973f8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/test/unionlimit1.sql
@@ -0,0 +1,90 @@
+#!sqlite3
+#
+# 2026-11-23
+#
+# The author disclaims copyright to this source code.  In place of
+# a legal notice, here is a blessing:
+#
+#    May you do good and not evil.
+#    May you find forgiveness for yourself and forgive others.
+#    May you share freely, never taking more than you give.
+#
+
+#***********************************************************************
+#
+# A compound SELECT whose rightmost operator is a UNION with LIMIT 1
+# may be coded by running the SELECTs to the left of the UNION first and
+# then the rightmost SELECT.  That shortcut is only valid if the left
+# part never needs a merge (only UNIONs, then UNION ALLs).  Otherwise:
+#
+#   *  The compound to the left is coded by its own sqlite3Select() call,
+#      which sends rows to the SRT_Table destination of a materialized
+#      subquery through multiSelectByMerge().  That routine does not
+#      handle SRT_Table, so the rows were returned as result rows of the
+#      outer statement instead (assert() in generateOutputSubroutine()
+#      on debug builds).
+#
+#   *  The compound to the left ignores collating sequences of SELECTs
+#      to the right, so an EXCEPT to the left uses the wrong collation.
+#
+.open :memory:
+.mode -reset list -colsep ' ' -rowsep ' '
+
+.testcase 100
+CREATE TABLE t1(a);
+INSERT INTO t1 VALUES(10),(20);
+.check ''
+
+.testcase 110
+SELECT * FROM t1 CROSS JOIN
+  (SELECT 1 INTERSECT SELECT 1 UNION SELECT 1 LIMIT 1);
+.check '10 1 20 1'
+
+.testcase 120
+SELECT count(*) FROM t1 CROSS JOIN
+  (SELECT 1 EXCEPT SELECT 2 UNION SELECT 3 LIMIT 1);
+.check '2'
+
+.testcase 130
+WITH c(x) AS MATERIALIZED (SELECT 5 INTERSECT SELECT 5 UNION SELECT 5 LIMIT 1)
+SELECT a, x FROM t1 CROSS JOIN c;
+.check '10 5 20 5'
+
+.testcase 140
+SELECT count(*) FROM t1 CROSS JOIN
+  (SELECT 1 UNION SELECT 2 UNION ALL SELECT 3 UNION SELECT 4 LIMIT 1);
+.check '2'
+
+# UNION and UNION ALL to the left of the UNION still use the shortcut
+#
+.testcase 150
+SELECT * FROM t1 CROSS JOIN
+  (SELECT 5 UNION ALL SELECT 6 UNION SELECT 7 LIMIT 1);
+.check '10 5 20 5'
+
+.testcase 160
+SELECT * FROM t1 CROSS JOIN
+  (SELECT 5 UNION SELECT 6 UNION SELECT 7 LIMIT 1);
+.check '10 5 20 5'
+
+.testcase 170
+EXPLAIN QUERY PLAN
+SELECT * FROM t1 CROSS JOIN
+  (SELECT 5 UNION ALL SELECT 6 UNION SELECT 7 UNION SELECT 8 LIMIT 1);
+.check -notglob '*MERGE*'
+
+# Collating sequences to the right apply to an EXCEPT to the left of
+# the UNION, also with LIMIT 1.
+#
+.testcase 200
+SELECT 'a' EXCEPT SELECT 'A' UNION SELECT 'x' COLLATE NOCASE LIMIT 1;
+.check 'x'
+
+.testcase 210
+.testctrl opt +All -UnionLimit
+SELECT 'a' EXCEPT SELECT 'A' UNION SELECT 'x' COLLATE NOCASE LIMIT 1;
+.check -glob '+All -UnionLimit x'
+
+.testcase 220
+.testctrl opt +All
+.check '+All'
